{"id":747,"name":"mareanie","speciesId":747,"dex":747,"form":"normal","generation":7,"types":["poison","water"],"stats":{"hp":50,"attack":53,"defense":62,"special-attack":43,"special-defense":52,"speed":45},"abilities":[{"name":"merciless","hidden":false},{"name":"limber","hidden":false},{"name":"regenerator","hidden":true}],"height":4,"weight":80,"baseExp":61,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/747.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/747.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/747.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/747.ogg","genus":"Brutal Star Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"sun","text":"It plunges the poison spike on its head into its prey. When the prey has weakened, Mareanie deals the finishing blow with its 10 tentacles."},{"version":"moon","text":"It’s found crawling on beaches and seafloors. The coral that grows on Corsola’s head is as good as a five-star banquet to this Pokémon."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"They eat Corsola branches, so Mareanie are hated by craftsmen who work with Corsola branches that have naturally fallen off."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"Aside from its head, its body parts regenerate quickly if they’re cut off. After a good night’s sleep, Mareanie is back to normal."},{"version":"sword","text":"The first symptom of its sting is numbness. The next is an itching sensation so intense that it’s impossible to resist the urge to claw at your skin."},{"version":"shield","text":"Unlike their Alolan counterparts, the Mareanie of the Galar region have not yet figured out that the branches of Corsola are delicious."}],"genderRate":4,"captureRate":190,"eggGroups":["water1"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"mareanie","speciesId":747,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions